        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The system is <b>completely transparent</b>: 11 = <tur>on bir</tur> (ten-one), 17 = <tur>on yedi</tur>, 23 = <tur>yirmi üç</tur>, 45 = <tur>kırk beş</tur>. And for hundreds: 100 = <tur>yüz</tur>, 1000 = <tur>bin</tur>, so 350 = <tur>üç yüz elli</tur>, 1985 = <tur>bin dokuz yüz seksen beş</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "text": "Age"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Question: <tur>Kaç yaşındasın?</tur> (how old are you?). Answer: <tur>Yirmi iki yaşındayım</tur> (I am 22 years old). Note the little particle <b>-da-</b> in the middle: « in my twenty-two years »."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "text": "Time"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The magic question: <tur>Saat kaç?</tur> (literally « hour how much? »). Structure: <tur>Saat</tur> + number. Then two useful words: <b>buçuk</b> (half past) and <b>çeyrek</b> (quarter)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Telling the time",
          "head": [
