    {
      "id": "m4",
      "num": 4,
      "level": "A1",
      "title": "Vowel harmony",
      "subtitle": "THE golden rule that explains 80% of Turkish grammar",
      "objectifs": [
        "Sort the vowels into two families",
        "Choose between a/e and i/ı/ü/u in a suffix",
        "Apply the rule automatically"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Here is the most valuable concept in all of Turkish. Vowels fall into <b>two families</b>: so-called « back » vowels and « front » vowels. The rule: <b>suffixes copy the family of the word's last vowel</b>. This is vowel harmony (<tur>ünlü uyumu</tur>): the language « sings » while staying consistent from start to finish."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The two vowel families",
          "head": [
            "BACK family",
            "FRONT family"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a, ı, o, u",
              "e, i, ö, ü"
            ],
            [
              "mouth rounded towards the back",
              "mouth towards the front"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "text": "Two-vowel harmony: a or e"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Some suffixes choose only between <b>a</b> and <b>e</b> (the plural, for example). If the word's last vowel is a back vowel → <b>a</b>; otherwise → <b>e</b>."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The plural -ler / -lar",
          "head": [
            "Word",
            "Last vowel",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>ev</tur> (house)",
              "e → front",
              "<tur>evler</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>masa</tur> (table)",
              "a → back",
              "<tur>masalar</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>köprü</tur> (bridge)",
              "ü → front",
              "<tur>köprüler</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>kitap</tur> (book)",
              "a → back",
              "<tur>kitaplar</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>göz</tur> (eye)",
              "ö → front",
              "<tur>gözler</tur>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "text": "Four-vowel harmony: i, ı, ü or u"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Other suffixes (such as -im « I am ») have 4 variants. The rule stays the same: look at the word's last vowel and copy its family and its rounding."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The suffix -im (I am…)",
          "head": [
            "Last vowel of the word",
            "Suffix",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "e or i",
              "-im",
              "<tur>öğretmenim</tur> (I am a teacher)"
            ],
            [
              "a or ı",
              "-ım",
              "<tur>hastayım</tur> (I am ill: with buffer y)"
            ],
            [
              "ö or ü",
              "-üm",
              "<tur>Türküm</tur> (I am Turkish)"
            ],
            [
              "o or u",
              "-um",
              "<tur>varım</tur> (I exist)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "warn",
          "tag": "Buffer",
          "text": "If the word ends in a vowel, a « buffer » consonant comes in between: <tur>hasta</tur> + -ım → hasta<b>y</b>ım (I am ill), <tur>öğrenci</tur> + -im → öğrenci<b>y</b>im (I am a student). Remember: final vowel → buffer y."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "text": "Your three-second method"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "<b>1.</b> Find the word's <b>last vowel</b> (ignore final consonants).",
            "<b>2.</b> Back family (a ı o u) → choose the « dark » variant of the suffix (a, ı, u).",
            "<b>3.</b> Front family (e i ö ü) → choose the « light » variant (e, i, ü)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "okul + lar → okullar",
              "fr": "the schools (u → back → lar)"
            },
            {
              "tr": "şehir + ler → şehirler",
              "fr": "the cities (i → front → ler)"
            },
            {
              "tr": "kadın + lar → kadınlar",
              "fr": "the women (ı → back → lar)"
            },
            {
              "tr": "gül + ler → güller",
              "fr": "the roses (ü → front → ler)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
